WEBVTT

00:55.806 --> 00:58.768
FILING FOR LOVE

02:29.775 --> 02:32.278
EPISODE 4:
PLAYING WITH FIRE

02:32.945 --> 02:33.946
FRIENDSHIP BEYOND PARTNERSHIP

02:34.029 --> 02:37.783
James is an innovator
who greatly advanced AI technology.

02:38.492 --> 02:39.577
It took great effort to invite him.

02:39.743 --> 02:40.953
FUTURE OF HAEMU'S TECH INNOVATION

03:02.725 --> 03:04.435
Ms. Joo must be at work by now.

03:05.769 --> 03:07.146
Let's avoid her as best I can today.

03:19.033 --> 03:20.701
Mr. Noh, Good morning.

03:20.910 --> 03:22.661
How come we meet right here?

03:22.745 --> 03:23.996
It's a small company, isn't it?

03:24.747 --> 03:27.082
It's your lucky day.
I'll treat you to a coffee.

03:27.166 --> 03:29.502
- No, I don't want...
- What is it? An Americano? A latte?

03:30.002 --> 03:31.462
Are you a die-hard
iced Americano fan?

03:32.880 --> 03:33.881
I am.

03:35.508 --> 03:36.509
What?

03:41.931 --> 03:43.849
How can she be so nonchalant?

03:44.767 --> 03:46.060
She must've seen me.

04:01.617 --> 04:04.119
Yes. I have to stay calm.

04:05.329 --> 04:06.705
Act natural

04:08.165 --> 04:09.250
like I always have.

05:01.885 --> 05:03.095
That James guy.

05:03.596 --> 05:05.264
He enjoys the spotlight too much.

05:05.931 --> 05:08.684
I get that scouting him
is your greatest achievement yet...

05:09.101 --> 05:10.686
Let's focus on the sport.

05:19.153 --> 05:20.571
That was a close miss.

05:21.196 --> 05:23.657
You almost got the last one.

05:23.741 --> 05:27.202
I'm getting so old,
I can't even pull a trigger.

05:27.286 --> 05:28.787
The shotgun is pretty hefty.

05:29.121 --> 05:30.164
Shall we switch to a pistol?

05:30.247 --> 05:31.790
Hitting a target is no fun.

05:32.041 --> 05:33.792
There's no prey and it's still.

05:35.044 --> 05:37.212
You're a true sniper at heart,
Father.

05:38.797 --> 05:40.591
The day you first took me hunting.

05:41.467 --> 05:42.885
That's when I decided.

05:43.469 --> 05:45.220
That I would be a good, obedient boy

05:45.596 --> 05:46.722
because my father's scary.

05:48.932 --> 05:50.100
You cheeky monkey.

05:51.727 --> 05:53.020
Why don't you two have a shoot-off?

05:53.437 --> 05:54.605
It's been a while since I watched.

06:21.382 --> 06:23.592
- It must've been like war.
- It was.

06:24.009 --> 06:26.178
The staff got worried
they would shoot each other.

06:27.012 --> 06:30.140
It looks like the time has come
to make up our minds

06:30.808 --> 06:32.643
about which of the two
we should root for.

06:33.310 --> 06:35.354
Don't you think our fate

06:35.437 --> 06:37.981
depends on who Ms. Joo sides with?

06:38.065 --> 06:40.359
I don't think
Ms. Joo will take sides.

06:40.442 --> 06:41.610
She's straight as an arrow.

06:42.820 --> 06:43.904
Mr. Ahn.

06:44.321 --> 06:46.240
Yes, I'm coming, Ms. Joo.

06:56.333 --> 06:58.502
How can I act like nothing happened?
It's just not the same.

07:00.713 --> 07:03.215
What kind of art studio
has such flimsy security?

07:03.298 --> 07:04.425
If they teach a class like that

07:04.967 --> 07:07.177
shouldn't they at least
lock the doors?

07:10.389 --> 07:13.267
You're saying Haemu Electronics'
Junior Engineer Lim Ha-kyong's case

07:14.351 --> 07:17.229
will be investigated
separately by the research center?

07:17.646 --> 07:19.690
Yes, it's a simple case

07:20.065 --> 07:22.401
so the center's HR department
will investigate

07:22.484 --> 07:24.903
and all we have to do
is review the report.

07:26.905 --> 07:27.948
We'll take this case.

07:28.031 --> 07:29.450
- I'll come with you.
- Okay.

07:29.533 --> 07:30.534
No, wait, what?

07:31.118 --> 07:33.245
You'll go and investigate yourself?

07:33.328 --> 07:35.831
Yes, since the new CTO
James Lockett joined

07:35.914 --> 07:38.792
they renovated the interior
to give it a Silicon Valley feel.

07:39.585 --> 07:41.670
Let's take a day-trip
to get some air and look around.

07:41.920 --> 07:44.882
But I have
a one-on-one meeting today.

07:44.965 --> 07:46.300
Oh, do you?

07:47.342 --> 07:49.470
In that case...

07:51.096 --> 07:53.849
Who wants to go
to the research center with me?

07:58.312 --> 08:00.898
Teams One and Two are
mostly at other subsidiaries

08:00.981 --> 08:03.776
for the routine audit season,
so they have no manpower to spare.

08:03.859 --> 08:05.402
Yes, you're right.

08:06.487 --> 08:10.908
Then who wants to with me
from Team Three?

08:11.241 --> 08:13.911
I've been under a lot of stress
due to a chain of events

08:13.994 --> 08:15.662
and my bowels are acting up. Sorry.

08:16.622 --> 08:17.915
Oh, no. I must dash.

08:21.835 --> 08:23.545
Any volunteers?

08:39.311 --> 08:42.272
Jeez, this is driving me crazy.

08:44.066 --> 08:45.108
All right.

08:45.651 --> 08:47.653
I might as well face her head-on.

08:50.322 --> 08:53.158
- So...
- Isn't it a lovely day?

08:54.284 --> 08:55.786
Yes, but Ms. Joo...

08:55.869 --> 08:58.205
Shall we have some udon noodles
at the rest area later?

08:58.789 --> 09:01.041
There was one place
with an awesome broth.

09:01.124 --> 09:04.169
I think it was the rest area
with trampolines for kids.

09:04.628 --> 09:06.547
- Ms. Joo, about yesterday...
- No! Don't talk.

09:07.965 --> 09:10.884
I need to concentrate
when I'm driving.

09:11.176 --> 09:12.719
I can't multitask

09:12.803 --> 09:14.388
so I can't drive if you talk.

09:14.847 --> 09:15.848
Let's go in silence.

09:17.724 --> 09:19.810
- Still, I...
- I told you not to speak.

09:19.893 --> 09:22.145
See? I almost missed the exit.

09:24.439 --> 09:26.024
You do all the talking.

09:36.410 --> 09:38.745
You charged 57,250 won
on the company card

09:39.329 --> 09:40.622
and have four strikes
for poor attitude.

09:45.961 --> 09:47.462
Read it slowly and carefully.

09:48.422 --> 09:49.464
Okay.

09:50.173 --> 09:52.175
CONFIRMATION OF AUDIT: LIM HA-KYONG

09:52.259 --> 09:53.468
Who did you upset?

09:56.889 --> 09:59.808
- Pardon?
- You were obviously targeted.

10:00.559 --> 10:02.185
The personal charges
on your company card.

10:02.686 --> 10:04.396
That happened too long ago
to penalize you now.

10:04.688 --> 10:05.856
Being five to ten minutes late?

10:05.939 --> 10:07.524
You don't report someone
to the head office

10:07.941 --> 10:09.985
for poor work ethics
for going to a bank.

10:12.571 --> 10:15.324
Who did you mess with

10:16.783 --> 10:19.453
that a junior engineer
would become a target?

10:23.582 --> 10:24.958
The Audit Team is
an independent department.

10:25.334 --> 10:27.210
You can speak freely,
without any concerns.

10:27.711 --> 10:29.296
Your secrets are safe with us.

10:39.765 --> 10:41.433
Well, actually...

10:53.320 --> 10:54.905
I wanted to meet you, Ms. Joo.

11:03.413 --> 11:04.581
Ms. Joo, Ha-kyong...

11:09.503 --> 11:10.504
Let's get it done quickly.

11:27.813 --> 11:28.814
Let's sit.

11:35.529 --> 11:36.780
Would you like to continue

11:37.906 --> 11:38.907
what you were saying earlier?

11:40.367 --> 11:41.368
What?

11:44.913 --> 11:46.039
I have nothing else to say.

11:47.541 --> 11:50.252
I'll just admit
to all the wrongdoings.

12:02.305 --> 12:03.724
Your coffees are here.

12:03.807 --> 12:05.517
- Oh, great.
- Thanks so much.

12:05.600 --> 12:07.185
- A hot Americano, right?
- Yes, thanks.

12:07.269 --> 12:08.353
- Thank you.
- Have a snack.

12:08.437 --> 12:09.438
- Okay.
- Thank you.

12:09.521 --> 12:10.897
I shall try this one.

12:11.982 --> 12:13.900
- That tastes really good.
- It's the famous...

12:13.984 --> 12:15.152
- Mr. Sung?
- Yes?

12:15.235 --> 12:17.320
When will you give me
this quarter's expenditure list?

12:17.487 --> 12:18.572
Hae-young.

12:19.114 --> 12:20.490
Let us be. It's Children's Day.

12:20.782 --> 12:23.452
- "Children's Day"?
- When the Head of Audit's away.

12:24.244 --> 12:26.121
When the Head of Audit is away

12:26.204 --> 12:28.749
- The world is ours for the taking
- The world is ours for the taking

12:30.584 --> 12:33.045
Since Ms. Joo's out,
I plan to take the afternoon off.

12:33.503 --> 12:34.963
Hey, what's wrong with you?

12:36.006 --> 12:37.132
You saw what Ms. Yoon did.

12:37.382 --> 12:38.842
She took this afternoon off
then canceled it.

12:39.051 --> 12:41.136
You shouldn't use paid time off
when your boss is away.

12:43.013 --> 12:44.097
That's the truth.

12:44.264 --> 12:46.808
I see there's so much more
for me to learn.

12:46.975 --> 12:50.854
- When do you need that by?
- Hello, everyone. Please excuse me.

12:51.188 --> 12:53.148
What brings you here,
Managing Director, sir?

12:54.024 --> 12:55.067
Oh, well...

12:55.817 --> 12:58.028
I should meet and greet
our Audit Team.

12:58.111 --> 12:59.321
You're pretty powerful people.

13:00.363 --> 13:03.158
Where's the star, Ms. Joo In-a?

13:03.241 --> 13:04.993
She's out of the office on business.

13:05.077 --> 13:06.203
It shouldn't take long.

13:06.286 --> 13:08.538
- She should be back today.
- Is that so?

13:09.706 --> 13:12.876
How about a team dinner
when Ms. Joo returns?

13:12.959 --> 13:14.544
It's gizzard shad season.

13:14.628 --> 13:16.713
Let's have some raw fish and soju.
It's my treat!

13:19.049 --> 13:22.636
- Mr. Jeon!
- Mr. Jeon!

13:22.719 --> 13:24.971
Okay. Text me
when you've made the reservation.

13:25.055 --> 13:26.556
- Yes, sir! Thank you!
- Thank you!

13:26.640 --> 13:28.058
- Thank you!
- Bye. We love you!

13:28.141 --> 13:29.226
- Work hard!
- Yes, sir!

13:32.604 --> 13:33.980
I should've taken the afternoon off.

13:34.606 --> 13:37.859
This must be the first team dinner
since he came back.

13:38.026 --> 13:40.278
Ms. Joo doesn't need to pick sides.

13:40.362 --> 13:41.947
Her side came looking for her.

13:42.280 --> 13:44.116
- Good for her.
- I should report to Ms. Joo.

13:44.908 --> 13:46.743
- He's so tall.
- I'm excited.

13:53.208 --> 13:54.209
Ms. Lim.

13:59.798 --> 14:02.342
I got the impression
you didn't tell us the full story.

14:03.635 --> 14:05.220
If you feel uneasy talking at work

14:06.012 --> 14:07.222
do you want to talk elsewhere?

14:11.935 --> 14:13.520
There's a phrase
the Audit Team quotes often.

14:14.271 --> 14:16.064
"Police, prosecutor,
judge, and attorney."

14:17.399 --> 14:20.193
We investigate like the police,
prosecute like a prosecutor

14:20.277 --> 14:21.695
make a ruling like a judge

14:22.404 --> 14:24.239
and defend the whistleblower
like an attorney.

14:25.824 --> 14:28.034
If you wish to report something to us

14:28.994 --> 14:30.120
from that moment on

14:30.745 --> 14:32.873
we will act as your attorneys.

14:33.540 --> 14:34.583
So...

14:36.251 --> 14:37.252
You can trust us.

14:39.171 --> 14:40.547
But you're still Haemu employees.

14:41.756 --> 14:42.966
I was told the same last time.

14:43.216 --> 14:45.552
That I should trust you and tell all.

14:45.927 --> 14:47.012
What?

14:54.936 --> 14:55.979
Ms. Lim.

14:59.524 --> 15:01.985
- Hello, Mr. Moo.
- Is Ms. Joo there with you?

15:02.402 --> 15:03.528
She's not answering her phone.

15:03.945 --> 15:05.363
I'm not with her right now.

15:06.406 --> 15:07.866
I'll get back to you.

15:08.533 --> 15:09.576
Okay, bye.

15:10.327 --> 15:11.369
Mr. Noh!

15:12.245 --> 15:15.373
Get over here.
There are lots of interesting things.

15:26.593 --> 15:28.220
How did you make something like this?

15:33.433 --> 15:35.185
We suspect him, too.

15:35.268 --> 15:37.479
His mind works
on a whole other level.

15:37.562 --> 15:39.940
Right. He mastered Korean in no time.

15:40.023 --> 15:41.107
He's a genius.

15:42.192 --> 15:44.694
Don't you flatter me like that.

15:51.868 --> 15:53.036
Okay, because over here...

15:53.119 --> 15:54.704
Sudden team dinner
with Managing Director Jeon.

15:54.955 --> 15:56.206
Inform Ms. Joo for me.

15:56.289 --> 15:57.374
A 100,000-won bet.

15:57.707 --> 15:58.708
- How's that?
- Ms. Joo.

16:10.512 --> 16:11.638
- Deal.
- Deal.

16:15.308 --> 16:17.435
Mr. Lee Seung-hyun is on
a New York business trip to prepare

16:17.519 --> 16:18.853
for the unpacking later this year.

16:19.312 --> 16:21.022
PR Team's Managing Director
Cheon Joo-won

16:21.106 --> 16:22.941
is increasing contact
with the media to influence

16:23.024 --> 16:25.193
how they report
our management issues.

16:25.277 --> 16:26.736
We're keeping an eye on Choi Woo-tae

16:26.820 --> 16:28.446
Haemu Chemicals' Vice CEO
who was rumored

16:28.530 --> 16:30.115
to have received
a job offer from overseas.

16:30.699 --> 16:32.242
How are things
between Directors Ma and Han?

16:32.492 --> 16:34.577
They seemed to be fighting over
which accounting firm to hire.

16:34.744 --> 16:36.705
They seem to have
reached an agreement.

16:36.788 --> 16:38.915
The Planning Team
will report to you soon.

16:40.333 --> 16:43.586
Managing Director Jeon seems
to have stepped in as a mediator.

16:45.046 --> 16:46.131
Sung-yeol?

16:46.923 --> 16:51.511
Yes, he has been meeting
the main executives in turn.

16:53.680 --> 16:54.764
He's working hard.

16:55.348 --> 16:56.474
This evening

16:57.058 --> 16:58.601
he's joining the Audit Team dinner.

16:59.686 --> 17:00.770
The Audit Team?

17:01.271 --> 17:02.647
Gosh, I'm exhausted.

17:02.731 --> 17:03.857
Ms. Park.

17:03.940 --> 17:05.442
What brings you to this lowly place?

17:05.525 --> 17:06.526
Hello.

17:07.027 --> 17:10.572
The vice president will attend
your team dinner as well.

17:10.655 --> 17:13.074
- What?
- He can't eat raw food

17:13.158 --> 17:15.201
so you should book a barbecue place.

17:15.285 --> 17:18.079
Pick one with a decent wine stock.

17:18.413 --> 17:20.540
Email me when you've found a place.

17:20.832 --> 17:21.916
Bye, then.

17:22.625 --> 17:23.752
- Okay.
- Okay.

17:24.336 --> 17:25.420
Goodbye.

17:28.048 --> 17:31.301
Why are we
suddenly at the center of attention?

17:31.801 --> 17:34.012
Managing Director Jeon... Oh, right.

17:35.347 --> 17:37.557
We booked a raw fish place.

17:37.640 --> 17:39.351
The managing director
wanted gizzard shad.

17:39.434 --> 17:42.771
- This is a disaster.
- No, wait.

17:43.313 --> 17:45.398
Team Three is in charge
of the booking.

17:45.899 --> 17:47.650
They should decide.

17:54.282 --> 17:55.450
Okay, everyone.

17:55.992 --> 17:58.244
Is it that serious an issue?

17:58.995 --> 18:01.456
The managing director said
he wanted gizzard shad

18:01.706 --> 18:03.958
and the vice president
can't eat raw fish.

18:04.084 --> 18:06.294
What someone can't eat
takes precedent over want.

18:06.378 --> 18:07.545
Don't you agree?

18:07.879 --> 18:09.255
I'll book a barbecue restaurant.

18:13.718 --> 18:14.844
Sorry.

18:14.928 --> 18:16.805
It's not that simple an issue.

18:16.888 --> 18:20.475
Hae-young, don't you see
how serious this matter is?

18:20.558 --> 18:23.478
The Audit Team's fate
depends on this decision.

18:23.561 --> 18:25.438
You can't be so rash.

18:26.106 --> 18:27.607
The managing director was first.

18:28.525 --> 18:29.609
Shall we have fish?

18:30.402 --> 18:32.404
His was the prior engagement.
That's a decent excuse.

18:34.239 --> 18:36.616
But the vice president
is higher in rank.

18:36.699 --> 18:38.535
That might be viewed as insolence.

18:41.454 --> 18:42.914
It's the biggest crisis of my career.

18:43.498 --> 18:44.624
Oh, dear...

18:59.973 --> 19:01.850
What do you think you're doing?

19:02.392 --> 19:04.644
There's definitely more
to this incident.

19:05.478 --> 19:07.272
You suspected she was targeted, too.

19:08.565 --> 19:11.234
We need to look into it.
We can't waste time playing golf.

19:19.284 --> 19:21.995
Don't you see
how hard I'm working right now?

19:38.219 --> 19:40.513
- Hello, Mr. Moo.
- Didn't you get my text?

19:41.014 --> 19:42.474
Whether we should have
barbecue or raw fish.

19:42.557 --> 19:43.808
Get her to decide for us.

19:44.392 --> 19:46.019
What's keeping Ms. Joo so busy?

19:47.979 --> 19:49.063
She's currently taking part

19:50.523 --> 19:52.192
in a global competition.

19:52.775 --> 19:54.777
What? She's doing a global what?

19:55.695 --> 19:57.489
Okay, fine. Bye.

19:58.323 --> 19:59.324
Oh, dear.

19:59.407 --> 20:00.408
Hasn't he asked her yet?

20:01.576 --> 20:03.077
We really need to make a booking now.

20:04.496 --> 20:06.748
This is so stressful.
What should we do?

20:09.834 --> 20:12.086
Look.
My hair's falling out from stress.

20:12.170 --> 20:13.671
What should I do now?

20:15.173 --> 20:18.051
Let's just eat both.

20:18.134 --> 20:19.135
Meat and raw fish.

20:19.511 --> 20:20.887
Are you suggesting a buffet?

20:20.970 --> 20:23.973
I looked them up,
and none of them serve both.

20:25.308 --> 20:26.351
You're wrong.

20:27.060 --> 20:29.062
The galbi place we had
last year's year-end party at.

20:29.812 --> 20:32.023
It's a barbecue restaurant,
but they also sell gizzard shad

20:32.106 --> 20:33.942
that the owner's mother-in-law
sends from Namhae.

20:34.400 --> 20:35.485
It's their seasonal offer.

20:36.611 --> 20:38.029
Hey, you're right.

20:38.112 --> 20:40.114
- Let me see.
- We found a place.

20:40.198 --> 20:41.199
Let me take a look.

20:41.282 --> 20:42.742
Why you... Take a look, sir.

20:44.244 --> 20:45.286
My word.

20:45.537 --> 20:46.996
Why are you sharing this now, Da-yae?

20:47.080 --> 20:48.831
You should've told us
before I started to lose hair.

20:55.838 --> 20:57.882
I had a great time, too, James.

20:58.383 --> 20:59.425
And also...

21:34.335 --> 21:37.463
Ms. Joo, your driver for hire
will take you back to Seoul.

21:37.547 --> 21:38.631
- Thanks.
- Sure.

21:39.173 --> 21:40.883
- Shall we?
- In-a, visit again.

22:01.362 --> 22:02.363
Hurry and get in the car.

22:02.447 --> 22:03.448
Move it. Hurry.

22:03.990 --> 22:06.075
Sir. Follow the car up ahead.

22:06.576 --> 22:07.869
I'll pay you
double the fare to Seoul.

22:07.952 --> 22:09.120
- Okay.
- Wear your seat belt.

22:23.593 --> 22:25.345
I knew it.

22:26.763 --> 22:28.181
We're following James, aren't we?

22:28.598 --> 22:30.933
Will you tell me now
what we did all day long?

22:31.476 --> 22:33.603
You didn't do all that
to befriend him, did you?

22:34.854 --> 22:36.272
Earlier at the research center.

22:37.106 --> 22:39.942
I looked up
James' company card statement.

22:41.402 --> 22:43.738
The company
got him a room at the Baron Hotel

22:44.530 --> 22:47.075
but he's been frequenting
the Rosa Hotel.

22:47.909 --> 22:48.993
So what?

22:49.243 --> 22:50.912
Do you suspect James?

22:50.995 --> 22:52.538
I suspected him from the start.

22:53.247 --> 22:55.541
The target
was a young female researcher.

22:55.625 --> 22:56.626
But James is...

22:57.418 --> 22:59.921
You know,
even if he's involved somehow

23:00.380 --> 23:02.173
the higher-ups
will try to cover it up.

23:02.757 --> 23:04.133
If this backfires
due to a careless move

23:04.217 --> 23:05.802
you could be in serious trouble.

23:06.177 --> 23:07.220
Exactly.

23:09.305 --> 23:10.473
I'll make sure it doesn't backfire.

23:47.802 --> 23:48.845
Mr. Noh.

23:49.595 --> 23:51.264
- Run.
- What?

23:52.974 --> 23:54.225
We need his room number.

23:54.767 --> 23:55.810
Get to it.

24:00.523 --> 24:01.607
Hang on.

24:48.404 --> 24:49.489
He got into the elevator.

24:50.156 --> 24:51.157
What floor are you on?

24:53.284 --> 24:54.327
The fifth floor.

24:55.077 --> 24:56.162
Still?

24:56.579 --> 24:57.663
Run faster.

24:58.080 --> 24:59.123
Excuse me?

25:01.667 --> 25:03.085
Jeez.

25:14.347 --> 25:15.515
Nine, ten.

25:19.685 --> 25:22.522
It's 13.
He got off at the 13th floor.

25:46.963 --> 25:49.298
I saw him enter Room 1307.

25:51.467 --> 25:52.802
Babe.

25:54.303 --> 25:56.097
Come here. Hurry.

25:57.723 --> 25:58.933
Yes, over here.

26:02.353 --> 26:04.230
Look at you sweating.

26:05.189 --> 26:07.275
Did you run so we could meet sooner?

26:11.404 --> 26:13.614
Oh, yes, right, sweetie.

26:14.490 --> 26:15.700
It's so hot.

26:17.451 --> 26:20.246
You make a lovely couple.

26:20.913 --> 26:22.248
Which room would you like?

26:22.540 --> 26:26.043
We have rooms
with a city view, a park view...

26:26.127 --> 26:27.295
Room 1306, please.

26:28.045 --> 26:30.089
- Pardon?
- The thing is...

26:31.757 --> 26:33.509
We're celebrating a special day.

26:34.343 --> 26:37.597
We want to reminisce
on what we did in Room 1306 before.

26:40.600 --> 26:41.893
Give me a moment.

26:42.018 --> 26:43.269
- Okay.
- So that's it.

26:45.187 --> 26:47.857
Oh, dear. I'm terribly sorry.

26:47.940 --> 26:51.569
Someone already checked into 1306

26:51.652 --> 26:54.113
and the room next door, 1307

26:54.196 --> 26:57.491
just became unavailable.

26:57.575 --> 26:59.035
What about Room 1308?

26:59.827 --> 27:02.330
Oh, that room is available, but...

27:02.914 --> 27:04.916
Since you're celebrating
a special day

27:04.999 --> 27:07.585
how about we offer you
a free upgrade?

27:07.668 --> 27:09.837
We're very proud of our suite...

27:09.921 --> 27:12.131
No, we'll take Room 1308.

27:13.299 --> 27:16.344
Our suite offers a much better view

27:16.802 --> 27:18.554
- that I'm sure...
- We want to be...

27:21.432 --> 27:23.851
as close to the special room
as possible.

27:31.817 --> 27:32.985
Give us that room.

27:33.361 --> 27:35.655
It means more to us than a room.

27:37.907 --> 27:39.075
It's such a special memory.

27:40.534 --> 27:42.620
Okay. Oh, gosh...

27:43.037 --> 27:45.915
I'll help you check in
as soon as possible.

27:48.542 --> 27:49.585
It's this way.

28:06.102 --> 28:07.812
You put on a great show earlier.

28:07.895 --> 28:09.230
Why are you hesitating now?

28:11.273 --> 28:12.358
You've already seen everything.

28:16.821 --> 28:17.989
Darn it.

28:45.391 --> 28:47.101
MOTHER-IN-LAW'S
SEASONAL GIZZARD SHAD FROM NAMHAE

28:50.730 --> 28:53.482
Shouldn't we seat the stepbrothers
across from each other?

28:53.816 --> 28:56.277
That will make this the top seat
and that would be weird.

28:56.485 --> 28:57.486
How about this layout?

28:57.737 --> 28:59.113
We separate the two tables

28:59.196 --> 29:01.407
so one has raw fish
and the other has barbecue.

29:01.490 --> 29:03.701
Wouldn't it be too obvious
that we separated them?

29:03.784 --> 29:04.785
- Right?
- Yes.

29:05.703 --> 29:07.038
This is a headache...

29:08.706 --> 29:10.249
You're here already.

29:10.750 --> 29:12.710
Hello and welcome, sir.

29:15.504 --> 29:18.758
Where should we seat you?

29:18.841 --> 29:20.384
Sit wherever you want, sir.

29:26.390 --> 29:28.100
What a bright idea
from our Gen Z employee.

29:35.941 --> 29:37.234
Okay. I'll sit here, then.

29:38.569 --> 29:39.779
Why not in the middle?

29:39.862 --> 29:42.490
No, this is fine.
I can see all of you from here.

29:42.573 --> 29:43.866
You can rotate after a while.

29:43.949 --> 29:45.034
Okay. We'll do that.

29:45.659 --> 29:46.869
The VP is here.

29:46.952 --> 29:48.162
- Hello, sir.
- Hello, sir.

29:48.245 --> 29:49.330
- Hello, sir.
- Hello, sir.

29:49.663 --> 29:52.875
What took you so long? I'm starving.

29:58.923 --> 30:00.466
- You can all sit down.
- Sure.

30:01.092 --> 30:02.426
Take a seat, everyone.

30:06.722 --> 30:07.765
Did I make you wait long?

30:07.848 --> 30:08.849
Gosh, no, sir.

30:08.933 --> 30:11.143
We just placed the order,
and they'll start serving.

30:11.560 --> 30:14.730
This is their wine list.
If there's anything you like...

30:14.814 --> 30:15.856
Jae-yeol.

30:16.148 --> 30:18.818
Don't drink wine. Soju is the drink
of choice for a team dinner.

30:18.901 --> 30:19.944
Aren't I right?

30:20.152 --> 30:22.071
Sure, soju sounds good.

30:22.154 --> 30:23.239
- Right?
- Yes.

30:25.324 --> 30:26.951
You can order whatever you like.

30:27.159 --> 30:28.160
Okay.

30:30.663 --> 30:32.123
I don't see Ms. Joo.

30:32.414 --> 30:34.250
Is she not back yet?

30:34.583 --> 30:36.293
Oh, I'll call and ask.

30:36.377 --> 30:38.170
- Call Mr. Noh.
- Okay.

30:38.546 --> 30:42.675
She's out on business
with Mr. Noh Ki-jun.

30:47.596 --> 30:48.681
It's so hot.

30:52.768 --> 30:54.270
Why are you undressing?

30:55.729 --> 30:58.190
I'm drenched in sweat
because you made me run the stairs

30:58.274 --> 30:59.608
to get the room number.

31:00.484 --> 31:01.569
So hot.

31:19.128 --> 31:21.005
- Hi, White Blood Cell.
- Mr. Noh.

31:21.088 --> 31:22.548
Are you with Ms. Joo?

31:25.301 --> 31:26.343
Yes, just a moment.

31:28.804 --> 31:29.930
It's Mr. Baek.

31:32.016 --> 31:33.976
- Yes, Mr. Baek?
- Ms. Joo.

31:34.393 --> 31:35.686
Where about are you?

31:36.020 --> 31:37.146
I'm in a hotel room.

31:39.148 --> 31:42.151
We're here for dinner
with the VP and MD.

31:42.234 --> 31:43.652
When can you get here?

31:43.736 --> 31:45.654
- I'm staying the night.
- What?

31:46.405 --> 31:48.657
- Pardon?
- Mr. Noh and I can't make it.

31:48.991 --> 31:51.160
- Send my regards to the bosses.
- Ms. Joo, it's...

31:52.119 --> 31:53.579
She hung up.

31:53.662 --> 31:54.872
What did she say?

31:55.956 --> 31:56.957
Well...

31:57.374 --> 32:01.420
Ms. Joo and Mr. Noh are in a hotel.

32:02.213 --> 32:04.632
They'll stay the night there.

32:06.342 --> 32:08.469
- Both of them?
- Yes.

32:11.555 --> 32:14.642
Ms. Joo, won't they get
the wrong idea if you say that?

32:16.393 --> 32:18.479
I couldn't say
we were spying on James.

32:19.146 --> 32:20.773
I only stated a fact.

32:21.148 --> 32:22.942
Yes, but still...

32:24.026 --> 32:25.027
Wait, I hear something.

32:27.780 --> 32:28.781
What's wrong?

32:34.453 --> 32:36.163
He's taking a shower.

32:36.664 --> 32:37.831
What?

32:37.915 --> 32:39.458
Okay, the rooms aren't soundproof.

32:39.959 --> 32:42.002
You can sit over here, Mr. Noh.

33:06.235 --> 33:07.361
Scoot over.

33:09.613 --> 33:11.740
You can't sit on a cold floor.

33:12.574 --> 33:13.575
Here you go.

33:31.218 --> 33:32.678
I'm so thirsty.

33:50.904 --> 33:52.114
This is a nice brand.

33:52.948 --> 33:54.825
I'll drink this
instead of getting paid extra.

33:55.451 --> 33:57.870
Are you really going to drink
in a hotel room?

33:58.954 --> 34:01.540
Yes, because I'm so thirsty,
all thanks to someone.

34:03.250 --> 34:05.627
What's wrong?
You said I've already seen it all.

34:20.184 --> 34:22.936
- That was delicious.
- It was so good. I'm full.

34:23.979 --> 34:25.272
Thank you for dinner, sir!

34:26.065 --> 34:28.108
- Thank you!
- Thank you, sir!

34:28.192 --> 34:29.610
- Hey, Min-su!
- Yes, sir!

34:29.985 --> 34:31.487
Let's play pool sometime soon.

34:31.570 --> 34:33.655
- Yes, and I won't let you win, sir.
- Please don't.

34:33.739 --> 34:36.033
Sir, you have to follow me back
on Instagram.

34:36.325 --> 34:38.327
Sure. No, while we're at it,
let me do it now.

34:38.410 --> 34:39.953
Really? Awesome!

34:40.037 --> 34:41.622
Sir, can you follow me, too?

34:41.705 --> 34:43.040
Wait a second.

34:43.624 --> 34:44.792
This is the kind of moment

34:45.959 --> 34:47.294
I really love.

34:48.962 --> 34:50.422
You're even funny!

34:50.506 --> 34:52.383
Follow me!

34:52.466 --> 34:54.218
Why don't we take a picture?

34:55.344 --> 34:57.137
- Get inside.
- Jump in!

34:57.221 --> 34:59.890
I'll take it now. One, two, three.

35:08.690 --> 35:10.109
- Mr. Choi.
- Yes?

35:10.192 --> 35:12.694
Let's stop by the pharmacy
for some headache pills.

35:12.778 --> 35:13.779
All right.

35:23.372 --> 35:24.623
I'll go and pick it up.

35:33.674 --> 35:34.925
What an immature day.

35:47.146 --> 35:48.230
Do I make you feel uncomfortable

35:49.606 --> 35:51.275
because of my feelings for you?

35:57.322 --> 35:58.407
Look at this right here.

35:59.783 --> 36:01.410
Park A-jeong.

36:02.161 --> 36:04.204
Your name is on the loan
as a guarantor.

36:04.663 --> 36:06.039
And there's your seal.

36:06.206 --> 36:07.583
I've never even seen this.

36:08.834 --> 36:10.210
This is a crime!

36:10.294 --> 36:12.171
Your older brother
is the one who conned us!

36:12.254 --> 36:15.549
The lease here and everything else
don't amount to half of what he owes!

36:16.258 --> 36:18.510
I gave him a good deal
because you had a good corporate job.

36:19.303 --> 36:21.013
Why don't you use this chance
to take on a new job?

36:21.889 --> 36:23.015
A pretty girl like you

36:23.098 --> 36:24.766
only needs a month
to pay back everything you owe.

36:43.994 --> 36:45.078
Mr. Vice President.

36:46.788 --> 36:47.789
Hello.

36:48.248 --> 36:49.625
My name is Park A-jeong

36:49.791 --> 36:51.793
the new executive assistant
from last week.

36:55.130 --> 36:57.257
I didn't expect you
to be at work this early.

36:57.341 --> 36:59.384
To be exact, I never went home.

37:00.802 --> 37:02.387
Why are you here already?

37:14.816 --> 37:17.861
I got this place
to occasionally spend time alone

37:19.530 --> 37:21.823
but I haven't had enough free time
to come here recently.

37:24.952 --> 37:26.703
Feel free to stick around
for as long as you want.

37:33.252 --> 37:35.087
I have most things you'll need.

37:37.839 --> 37:39.758
But there's no food or water.

37:46.890 --> 37:47.891
Do you want a drink?

38:07.828 --> 38:08.870
Have a seat.

38:14.793 --> 38:16.336
Let's skip this nonsense

38:17.170 --> 38:18.297
and cut to the chase.

38:19.006 --> 38:20.257
Do you want to shower first?

38:21.466 --> 38:22.718
Or should I wash up first?

38:25.137 --> 38:26.179
What's wrong?

38:27.848 --> 38:29.433
Are you into something specific?

38:52.748 --> 38:54.082
Just accept someone's kindness

38:58.211 --> 38:59.963
as kindness itself.

39:06.595 --> 39:08.013
If you think it's too much

39:09.348 --> 39:10.974
think of it as an employee benefit.

39:26.323 --> 39:29.284
Yes, the product is innovative.

39:29.743 --> 39:32.663
However, it's hard for me
to see the roadmap

39:32.746 --> 39:34.665
in the mid to long-term perspective.

39:36.541 --> 39:38.710
To include this in Haemu's portfolio

39:38.794 --> 39:40.379
not only do we need a good idea

39:40.754 --> 39:42.881
but we need to see
a specific execution plan.

39:44.758 --> 39:45.801
Yes.

39:47.010 --> 39:50.347
Yes, I'll check the vice president's
schedule and get back to you.

39:51.223 --> 39:52.265
Sure.

40:24.923 --> 40:26.049
I got a bit drunk.

40:27.884 --> 40:29.344
I have a question.

40:33.140 --> 40:34.683
What are you

40:35.308 --> 40:36.351
so tormented by?

40:37.352 --> 40:39.312
You never eat but only drink alcohol

40:39.771 --> 40:41.440
never sleep, and only work.

40:42.315 --> 40:44.025
If I were as rich as you

40:45.652 --> 40:47.779
I would only eat good food
and go out all the time.

41:08.175 --> 41:09.176
I know that was a mistake.

41:10.010 --> 41:11.219
It's late. You should go.

41:13.221 --> 41:14.473
It wasn't a mistake.

41:17.684 --> 41:18.935
I like you.

41:20.771 --> 41:21.813
Mr. Jeon.

41:22.689 --> 41:24.274
And it's not because I'm drunk.

41:24.858 --> 41:27.152
And no, it's not
because of what you have.

41:27.235 --> 41:28.528
I don't expect anything in return.

41:29.613 --> 41:31.156
I understand your situation

41:31.990 --> 41:33.283
and I already know my place.

41:35.285 --> 41:36.286
I just

41:38.747 --> 41:40.123
wanted to share

41:41.124 --> 41:42.125
how I felt.

41:44.795 --> 41:46.046
I'll pretend like I never heard it.

42:26.795 --> 42:27.963
What happened in the art class

42:29.881 --> 42:30.924
is more embarrassing for me.

42:33.510 --> 42:35.345
"Should I go and kill myself?"

42:36.763 --> 42:38.348
"No, should I kill Mr. Noh instead?"

42:39.474 --> 42:40.892
I went back and forth
millions of times.

42:42.936 --> 42:43.979
I knew it.

42:44.813 --> 42:46.940
- You were just acting chill.
- Yes.

42:51.278 --> 42:52.279
Jeez.

42:59.828 --> 43:01.121
I'm sorry, anyway.

43:02.330 --> 43:04.249
You must feel like you were violated.

43:04.875 --> 43:06.001
After all, I was the intruder.

43:08.086 --> 43:10.130
You had no idea when you came
to the art class, anyway.

43:10.922 --> 43:11.965
Sorry?

43:14.301 --> 43:16.011
Yes, right.
The recreational art class.

43:16.636 --> 43:18.471
Tell me about it.
What are the chances?

43:23.476 --> 43:25.979
Let me make this clear
in case you thought I had two jobs.

43:26.271 --> 43:27.480
I don't get paid to do that.

43:27.564 --> 43:29.149
It's like a hobby.

43:30.233 --> 43:31.526
Yes, sure.

43:32.152 --> 43:34.362
Something like a different job
didn't even cross my mind.

43:34.946 --> 43:36.197
I couldn't think in that situation.

43:46.875 --> 43:47.918
Anyway

43:49.878 --> 43:50.921
may I ask you this?

43:54.674 --> 43:55.842
Why did you take up that hobby?

44:01.264 --> 44:02.849
That way, I can breathe.

44:06.603 --> 44:07.687
I mean, you know.

44:08.146 --> 44:09.689
Every office worker
needs something like that.

44:09.773 --> 44:11.358
A place to breathe.

44:12.108 --> 44:13.151
That's why.

44:54.317 --> 44:55.318
But wait.

44:55.777 --> 44:56.778
How are your feet so tiny?

44:57.362 --> 44:58.947
What? My feet?

45:01.282 --> 45:02.575
No, yours are just huge.

45:04.703 --> 45:05.787
I don't think so.

45:32.022 --> 45:33.148
Could you stop staring at my body?

45:33.440 --> 45:34.482
What?

45:35.483 --> 45:36.818
Goodness, how can you say that?

45:38.403 --> 45:39.529
I also suffered

45:40.196 --> 45:42.115
from a great psychological shock!

45:43.241 --> 45:44.784
Are you saying my body was shocking?

45:44.951 --> 45:45.952
Yes, of course!

45:48.455 --> 45:49.748
No, wait.

45:50.165 --> 45:52.375
I don't mean that in a bad way.

45:52.459 --> 45:54.335
What I want to tell you is that

45:54.419 --> 45:56.755
- it was shocking in a good way...
- So you liked it?

45:57.797 --> 46:00.383
I mean, if I say I liked it

46:00.467 --> 46:02.218
it can lead
to another misunderstanding.

46:02.302 --> 46:03.803
What I want to say is this.

46:04.304 --> 46:05.972
What I meant was...

46:10.935 --> 46:13.063
So, now what? What do you want?

46:14.105 --> 46:16.441
Should I just strip naked right now?
That will be fair.

46:16.524 --> 46:18.026
- That's a great idea.
- What?

46:18.610 --> 46:19.694
Are you serious right now?

46:21.863 --> 46:23.990
Gosh, I can't deal with this.

46:25.283 --> 46:26.326
Watch out!

46:53.603 --> 46:54.687
Sorry?

47:55.623 --> 47:57.083
The Audit Team
from the head office is here.

47:59.794 --> 48:01.546
Why are you causing trouble
for everyone?

48:27.447 --> 48:29.657
You're breaking my heart.

48:30.700 --> 48:31.826
Don't be so uptight.

48:32.744 --> 48:33.995
No need to make a big deal out of it.

48:59.479 --> 49:03.066
Remember our forehead smack bet?
I won that bet.

49:03.691 --> 49:05.985
I wouldn't call that a smack.
That was a punch.

49:22.835 --> 49:24.420
He asked for a meeting.

49:26.047 --> 49:28.049
He had something to ask
about the research data.

49:29.884 --> 49:31.970
I was concerned
that it was held at a hotel.

49:33.054 --> 49:34.806
But that's where he had been staying

49:35.431 --> 49:36.641
and I heard

49:37.350 --> 49:38.810
he often held meetings there.

49:41.271 --> 49:42.605
It was my mistake.

49:42.814 --> 49:44.816
You didn't make a mistake, Ms. Lim.

49:45.358 --> 49:46.526
Please don't blame yourself.

49:49.779 --> 49:51.197
What are you going to do?

49:51.281 --> 49:53.074
We were really ordered to do this.

49:53.157 --> 49:54.200
We're unfairly blamed!

49:54.701 --> 49:57.161
It's James, Ms. Joo. James...

50:09.090 --> 50:11.217
- Thank you.
- You don't have to thank me.

50:11.301 --> 50:12.635
The Audit Team did what it had to do.

50:43.541 --> 50:44.751
She must be exhausted.

50:52.091 --> 50:55.094
QUICK CONTROL

51:15.907 --> 51:17.033
I have a question.

51:17.909 --> 51:19.744
During Mr. Son's infidelity case

51:20.119 --> 51:22.288
both Mr. Son
and Ms. Jeong were at fault

51:22.622 --> 51:24.374
but you only let Mr. Son stay
in the head office.

51:24.874 --> 51:27.210
- Yes.
- You said he was crucial to us.

51:28.378 --> 51:29.837
You said morals were different
in the office

51:29.921 --> 51:32.173
and we only had to care
about how it affects our company.

51:33.674 --> 51:36.636
But James is way more crucial
than Mr. Son.

51:37.345 --> 51:38.930
Why did you take things this far?

51:41.557 --> 51:42.642
Isn't it obvious?

51:43.518 --> 51:44.602
That was a crime.

51:50.900 --> 51:52.193
He's expecting you.

51:54.862 --> 51:57.073
You can wait here, Mr. Noh.
I'll report to him.

52:11.045 --> 52:13.548
You two must've grown close.

52:14.966 --> 52:18.428
I mean, you're standing here
like a puppy protecting its owner.

52:19.262 --> 52:20.805
You used to say
a lot of bad things about her.

52:21.222 --> 52:22.265
Are you picking a fight?

52:24.308 --> 52:25.393
I don't appreciate

52:26.144 --> 52:27.728
you staying the night out
without notice.

52:29.021 --> 52:32.024
Hey, I didn't stay the night out.
And that's my home.

53:50.353 --> 53:51.479
Hey, you're late.

53:51.729 --> 53:52.772
Do you want a drink?

53:59.904 --> 54:01.948
What's wrong with the vice president?

54:02.573 --> 54:04.075
He looked like a pretty chill guy.

54:05.451 --> 54:08.162
I've never seen him
like that, either.

54:09.205 --> 54:11.707
- It's James we're talking about.
- But still.

54:12.083 --> 54:13.793
He sexually assaulted
his junior staff member

54:13.876 --> 54:16.170
and even conducted a targeted audit
when she reported him.

54:16.254 --> 54:19.340
Who cares if he's James or Zeus?
We have to kick him out!

54:19.423 --> 54:20.883
Why are you so invested in this?

54:21.300 --> 54:23.761
You've never been interested
in justice.

54:24.679 --> 54:26.264
I'm not talking about justice.

54:26.639 --> 54:29.225
We're talking
about common sense, okay?

54:29.976 --> 54:32.228
Now that
we're talking about common sense...

54:34.146 --> 54:36.649
Last night,
what did you and Joo-In-a do

54:36.983 --> 54:39.860
all alone in that room

54:40.653 --> 54:41.946
throughout the night?

54:42.530 --> 54:43.698
What? What about it?

54:43.864 --> 54:45.366
I mean, it's common sense.

54:45.449 --> 54:47.952
A man and a woman
spent a night in a hotel room.

54:49.245 --> 54:50.329
Isn't that weird?

54:57.211 --> 54:59.088
Hey, we were there to work.
Can't you see?

54:59.422 --> 55:00.715
We caught a big fish like him.

55:00.798 --> 55:02.049
I'm sure you two worked.

55:02.341 --> 55:05.219
But did you spend
the entire time just working?

55:07.346 --> 55:09.098
So nothing happened?

55:14.395 --> 55:16.522
- Something happened.
- Nothing happened.

55:17.231 --> 55:20.526
I was stunned for a second
because your argument was so absurd.

55:23.779 --> 55:25.156
What's wrong with you?

55:26.782 --> 55:27.867
Wash up and go to sleep.

55:52.308 --> 55:54.101
Ms. Joo, the final report on James.

56:12.953 --> 56:14.163
Now, this one.

56:15.414 --> 56:17.917
Look at the scope of audit.

56:18.542 --> 56:19.585
Yes.

56:21.337 --> 56:22.505
Take a look at it.

56:33.933 --> 56:35.101
It looks good on you.

56:38.646 --> 56:39.730
Thank you for that.

57:22.440 --> 57:24.233
REPORTING MS. JOO IN-A

57:32.158 --> 57:33.743
SHE IS INVOLVED IN AN INAPPROPRIATE
WORKPLACE RELATIONSHIP

57:36.912 --> 57:38.164
I ATTACH THE EVIDENCE

58:16.368 --> 58:17.369
Mr. Noh.

58:19.914 --> 58:21.290
Are you not coming
to the class today?

58:21.624 --> 58:23.417
We're not doing quick sketches today.

58:25.669 --> 58:28.714
And I forgot to make myself clear.

58:29.381 --> 58:31.050
I don't mind having you there.

58:31.801 --> 58:33.427
Those classes happen
only from time to time

58:33.636 --> 58:35.596
and I can stop being the model.

58:37.014 --> 58:38.057
It's all right.

58:38.766 --> 58:41.477
It's fine by me, too.
Feel free to show up comfortably.

58:49.318 --> 58:50.569
I don't feel comfortable.

58:51.028 --> 58:52.238
And I have no reason to be there.

59:07.545 --> 59:08.587
Hey.

59:09.046 --> 59:11.006
You're not allowed to drink here.

59:11.090 --> 59:12.216
Don't be a nightmare.

59:13.217 --> 59:14.802
This is alcohol-free.

59:16.262 --> 59:18.597
Anyway, why are you here?

59:23.936 --> 59:24.937
No particular reason.

59:25.688 --> 59:26.981
I had no one to talk to.

59:27.147 --> 59:28.274
Don't you have any friends?

59:29.358 --> 59:30.484
Poor guy.

59:32.361 --> 59:33.404
Do you want to drink with me?

59:34.780 --> 59:36.448
Don't say something like that.

59:37.074 --> 59:38.450
Don't trust random guys out there

59:38.534 --> 59:39.952
and drink with them
like it's nothing.

59:40.119 --> 59:42.788
You need to be wary of them
and be cautious in this foreign land.

59:42.872 --> 59:43.998
Why are you taking this out on me?

59:44.081 --> 59:45.541
- What?
- Is your life in turmoil?

59:45.958 --> 59:47.001
What's with you?

59:47.418 --> 59:49.003
Have you still not found

59:49.461 --> 59:50.588
the pretty girl's man?

59:52.882 --> 59:54.508
I don't know who he is yet

59:56.343 --> 59:58.637
- but I've made progress.
- No way!

59:58.929 --> 01:00:00.139
Congrats, man.

01:00:00.639 --> 01:00:02.391
You said you had to find him

01:00:02.474 --> 01:00:03.976
to keep doing your job smoothly.

01:00:04.393 --> 01:00:05.519
Isn't that good news?

01:00:07.438 --> 01:00:08.480
It is.

01:00:09.815 --> 01:00:10.858
It's great for me.

01:00:10.941 --> 01:00:13.777
So why are you so annoyed?
It's great news.

01:00:16.780 --> 01:00:17.823
I wonder.

01:00:20.492 --> 01:00:22.286
Why am I so annoyed?
It's so annoying.

01:00:42.014 --> 01:00:43.015
Thank you for that.

01:04:41.086 --> 01:04:42.713
Have I always been this pretty?

01:04:44.882 --> 01:04:45.924
Right?

01:05:03.942 --> 01:05:04.943
You are pretty.

01:06:31.488 --> 01:06:34.408
FILING FOR LOVE

01:07:02.769 --> 01:07:04.771
A kiss definitely makes it official.

01:07:04.855 --> 01:07:05.856
I apologize.

01:07:05.939 --> 01:07:08.108
I shouldn't have done that
as your superior.

01:07:08.191 --> 01:07:10.235
- Like I was under a magic spell.
- Was she the only one who kissed?

01:07:10.319 --> 01:07:11.695
Why does she decide everything
on her own?

01:07:11.778 --> 01:07:12.946
Even after the kiss

01:07:13.030 --> 01:07:14.906
I thought an apology
would settle everything.

01:07:16.283 --> 01:07:18.076
I want to know

01:07:18.160 --> 01:07:19.369
if there's something more between us.

01:07:20.203 --> 01:07:21.204
Do you want to sleep with me?

01:07:21.413 --> 01:07:22.414
Do you?

01:07:24.041 --> 01:07:25.625
Can it really happen?

01:07:25.709 --> 01:07:26.877
Can you really fall for someone

01:07:27.711 --> 01:07:29.379
you've known for so long?

01:07:42.392 --> 01:07:44.394
Subtitles by Eunsook Youn
and Jennifer Lim
